<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Under der linden</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Under der linden&quot; is a well-known poem by the medieval German lyric poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walther-von-der-vogelweide">Walther von der Vogelweide</a>, written in Middle High German. It was a song: its four strophes are preserved in only two <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a>, the Weingarten Manuscript and the Manesse Codex. Neither manuscript holds a melody, so the tune Walther's audience heard is not known.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>&quot;<b>Under der linden</b>&quot; is a well-known poem by the medieval German lyric poet Walther von der Vogelweide, written in Middle High German.</blockquote><a href="/songs/under-der-linden">Under der linden</a></li></ul></section>
